# Derived propositions of PM I, ✱54

The 34-item catalogue is present, but no ✱54 theorem can yet be replayed honestly in
`Derivation`.  Its first two definitions use class abstractions as values
(`0 = ιʻΛ` and the class `2`).  In the ramified syntax, ✱20·01 is correctly a
contextual `incompleteScope`, not a `Term`; the deduction judgement currently
has no derived definition-elimination theorem connecting that scope to the
identity formula of ✱13·01.  The earliest cited derived dependencies (notably
✱51·41 and ✱51·43) are likewise not exposed as ramified derivations.

Consequently this module records no theorem declaration.  Replacing the
printed formula by a host-logic statement, or assuming the desired assertion
as a Lean premise, would violate the certification contract.
-/

